  "body": "Most new homes in Ara Hills are built to a budget. This one is built to be lived in, with 161m² (approx.) of thoughtfully planned space and the finishes to match.\r\n\r\nAt its centre is the open-plan kitchen, dining and living area. The living flows straight out to a private deck for long summer evenings and weekend entertaining.\r\n\r\nThe main bedroom is a retreat of its own, with an ensuite and walk-in wardrobe. Two further bedrooms share a family bathroom, and a built-in study nook gives you a spot for homework or working from home.\r\n\r\nComfort is built in year-round, with ducted heating & air conditioning and under-floor heating in the bathrooms. Outside, the cedar and weatherboard exterior and easy-care landscaping mean less time on upkeep and more time enjoying the home.\r\n\r\n* 161m² (approx.) floor area on 324m² (approx.) freehold\r\n* 3 bedrooms + study nook\r\n* 2 bathrooms, including ensuite\r\n* Open-plan living with indoor-outdoor flow to the deck\r\n* Ducted heating & air conditioning\r\n* Single garage plus off-street parking\r\n* In zone for Orewa Primary and Orewa College \r\n\r\nAra Hills sits right off the Grand Drive interchange, about 3km from Orewa village. The development borders the Nukumea Reserve, so bush walks are part of everyday life.",
